WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.940
The entire Foundation was in turmoil; researchers&nbsp;
were getting into heated fistfights with security&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:11.340
officers, who in turn were retaliating in&nbsp;
fits of unbridled, animalistic rage. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:16.200
facility had erupted into such a frenzy, with&nbsp;
chairs being hurled across testing chambers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:21.540
and armories raided for weapons to escalate&nbsp;
the brawl into a far deadlier incident.&nbsp;

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:27.240
Tables were overturned and used as cover as the&nbsp;
Foundation’s own staff turned on each other,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:33.060
and before long, an all-out war had erupted. But&nbsp;
this wasn’t a battle of one side versus another,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:38.760
no this was a wild and rampant free for all.&nbsp;
Everyone was out to get everyone else, viewing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:45.960
their own colleagues as mortal enemies. And it was&nbsp;
all thanks to Junior… the spawn of the Shy Guy!&nbsp;

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:50.760
Only a month before, the Foundation had&nbsp;
been subject to another bout of chaos,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:55.440
although this one was much more subdued than&nbsp;
the explosive battle that would later sweep the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.440 --> 00:01:01.500
facility. Everyone was abuzz, researchers ignored&nbsp;
their work, and some security personnel even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:08.820
abandoned their posts to see what all the fuss&nbsp;
was about: something was very wrong with SCP-096.&nbsp;

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:14.640
The creature was normally docile unless directly&nbsp;
observed. It spent the majority of its time just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:18.900
pacing around its containment chamber or&nbsp;
staying hunched over in a fetal position,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:24.360
crying to itself. In fact, it was so often&nbsp;
sobbing quietly and making all manner of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:29.460
discontented noises that this became&nbsp;
known as its usual behavior. At first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:34.380
almost nobody had noticed that something was&nbsp;
even amiss, all seemed right with the miserable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:41.040
monster… that is, until the screaming started.
It was a loud, shrieking sound that pierced the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:46.200
eardrums of whoever heard it, then proceeded to&nbsp;
climb down their spine to bring a chill to their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:52.920
bones, make their blood run icy cold, and cause&nbsp;
their skin to be littered with goosebumps. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:58.680
screeching, disturbing noise flooded out of&nbsp;
SCP-096’s cell, reverberating off every wall&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:04.560
and echoing down every corridor until not one&nbsp;
member of Foundation personnel could ignore it.&nbsp;

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:09.840
It was unlike anything they’d ever heard from&nbsp;
the creature before, this primal howling seemed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:15.060
to put everyone who heard it on edge. Not just&nbsp;
because it was unfamiliar, but because everyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:21.840
uncannily seemed to know what the screams were&nbsp;
indicating: pain. Perhaps even the worst physical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:28.740
pain that SCP-096 had ever felt. What if the&nbsp;
Shy Guy was dying? Something had to be done.&nbsp;

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:34.620
But therein lay a hurdle to clear first: how could&nbsp;
the Foundation help, even offer medical assistance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:39.840
if needed, to a creature they couldn’t even safely&nbsp;
look at? What options are there for even getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:44.880
somebody close enough to examine the Shy Guy&nbsp;
without it killing them? They were limited,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:49.920
but a crowd of the SCP Foundation’s best and&nbsp;
brightest researchers had already congregated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:55.500
outside the containment chamber housing&nbsp;
SCP-096 after they’d heard its screams. Surely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.500 --> 00:03:01.380
between them, they could come up with an idea.
Hearing the Shy Guy continuing to howl in agony,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:06.480
one researcher came forward and made a suggestion.&nbsp;
There was a device that another Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:11.940
researcher had developed, codenamed ‘SCRAMBLE’.&nbsp;
Resembling standard issue night vision goggles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:17.640
one Doctor Dan had created these ‘SCRAMBLE&nbsp;
Goggles’ to identify SCP-096’s face and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:23.640
digitally alter it so that the wearer was&nbsp;
unable to see it. Essentially, it edited out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:28.800
the Shy Guy’s face in real time, so that its&nbsp;
homicidal rage state couldn’t be activated.&nbsp;

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:34.380
The use of Doctor Dan’s SCRAMBLE Goggles had&nbsp;
previously led to a catastrophic incident that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:40.200
claimed the lives of Mobile Task Force Tau-1,&nbsp;
also known as Big Brother. The SCRAMBLE devices&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:46.380
allowed the wearer’s brain to receive a single&nbsp;
nanosecond of SCP-096 unscrambled before the image&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:51.540
was altered by the goggles. So, needless to say,&nbsp;
since time was running out to help the creature,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:55.620
and there were no other viable options for&nbsp;
doing so, the SCRAMBLE Goggles would need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.620 --> 00:04:00.060
some serious refinement – and fast!
Working as quickly as they could,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:05.220
the gathered gaggle of researchers requisitioned&nbsp;
an old pair of SCRAMBLE Goggles and started&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:09.120
trying to improve them. Tirelessly tinkering&nbsp;
equipment specialists put their heads together&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:15.420
with computing engineers as they coded crazily,&nbsp;
all underscored by the continued screams of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:21.540
SCP-096. Then, without warning or even any&nbsp;
hint of what had happened inside the cell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:26.760
the screaming suddenly stopped. Everyone outside&nbsp;
the containment chamber stopped for a second,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:32.940
falling deathly silent. The goggles were almost&nbsp;
ready, but were they too late to save the Shy Guy?&nbsp;

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:37.980
The security personnel who had also gathered&nbsp;
in response to the sound all drew straws,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:42.540
with the officer pulling the shortest being the&nbsp;
one tasked with venturing into the containment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:47.640
chamber. He was handed the goggles and instructed&nbsp;
that they would blur his vision entirely for a few&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:52.980
seconds while the SCRAMBLE software had a chance&nbsp;
to work. Then, once the device had double, triple,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:58.200
and quadruple-checked the results, the goggles&nbsp;
would activate fully and – in theory – work&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:03.300
the way Doctor Dan had originally intended.&nbsp;
Although, the track record of the SCRAMBLE&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:08.820
project meant the officer was hardly reassured as&nbsp;
he entered the dark, dingy containment chamber.&nbsp;

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:13.740
He couldn’t see a thing ahead of him, his vision&nbsp;
totally obscured as the goggles started running&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:18.720
the newly updated version of the SCRAMBLE&nbsp;
software. They were untested, so naturally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:24.180
the security officer’s nerves were at peak levels,&nbsp;
worried the device might fail, and any second,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:31.020
his eyes would be greeted by the face of SCP-096.&nbsp;
He could tell the creature was still alive; there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:36.180
was a low sound of panting breaths coming from the&nbsp;
far corner of the chamber, indicating it hadn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:40.500
perished, although it might have been injured.
A sudden bleep from the SCRAMBLE Goggles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:45.000
startled the officer – the device had made&nbsp;
its checks and was ready to activate. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:48.420
an unexpected message blinked on&nbsp;
the heads-up display, that read:&nbsp;

00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:53.940
“Warning: multiple subjects detected.”
Luckily enough, when the goggles activated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.940 --> 00:06:00.360
the officer was relieved to see they had worked.&nbsp;
SCP-096’s face was a grainy, pixelated mess.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:05.760
The creature showed little noticeable sign of any&nbsp;
injuries too and just seemed to be gently rocking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:12.300
itself in the corner. But quickly, the reason –&nbsp;
and perhaps even the cause – of SCP-096’s earlier&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:17.100
screams soon became obvious: though nobody&nbsp;
had entered the containment cell before the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:23.640
security officer, it seemed the Shy Guy wasn’t&nbsp;
alone. Standing at around a third of SCP-096’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:29.220
considerable height… was another Shy Guy.
Or, at least, another version, a creature almost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:35.640
identical save for being shorter. It wobbled on&nbsp;
its elongated legs, like it wasn’t quite used to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:42.120
standing upright. It kept both arms outstretched&nbsp;
towards SCP-096, almost as though it was reaching&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:46.920
out for a hug. But the Shy Guy stayed in the&nbsp;
corner, cowering away from the other creature.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:51.360
Through his scramble goggles, the security&nbsp;
officer looked on in disbelief at the scene&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.360 --> 00:07:00.780
before him. Somehow, completely unpredictably,&nbsp;
SCP-096 had spawned offspring. It’d had a baby.&nbsp;

00:07:00.780 --> 00:07:04.860
There was a general air of disbelief&nbsp;
among the assembled staff outside the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:09.300
containment chamber after the security officer&nbsp;
had relayed what had happened. Most were quick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:15.060
to write it off as an impossibility; they’d&nbsp;
studied SCP-096 for a long time, and it had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.060 --> 00:07:20.400
been the only anomaly known to the Foundation&nbsp;
matching its own very particular description.&nbsp;

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:25.740
There had been no others sighted in the wild,&nbsp;
it didn’t seem to be part of a species, as far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:31.560
as anyone knew. But other researchers refuted&nbsp;
this claim; given SCP-096’s ability to travel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:37.200
at anomalous speeds and kill those that looked&nbsp;
at it, it stood to reason there could be others.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:42.600
Maybe the Foundation wasn’t aware of a whole&nbsp;
species of Shy Guys because anyone who’d ever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:48.420
seen one didn’t live long enough to report it.
Then someone mentioned that it wasn’t entirely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.420 --> 00:07:52.860
unprecedented for anomalies to have&nbsp;
offspring, either. A long while before,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.860 --> 00:08:00.420
SCP-049 – the infamous beak-masked Plague Doctor –&nbsp;
had laid an egg which had hatched into SCP-049-J,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.260 --> 00:08:07.140
a smaller version of himself composed of moss&nbsp;
and wads of tissue. Trying to apply logical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.140 --> 00:08:11.520
understanding to each and every anomaly&nbsp;
was a paradoxical exercise in futility:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:16.980
all anomalies had their own rules, even rules&nbsp;
the Foundation had never observed before.&nbsp;

00:08:16.980 --> 00:08:22.140
After a great deal of deliberation and additional&nbsp;
improvements of the SCRAMBLE technology,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:28.620
a research team was sent into the containment&nbsp;
chamber to retrieve SCP-096’s progeny. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.620 --> 00:08:33.420
parent creature was still shying away from its&nbsp;
creation, perhaps because it didn’t want to raise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.420 --> 00:08:38.820
it in a way that meant the child inherited its&nbsp;
deadly sense of self-consciousness. Then again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:45.060
maybe the Shy Guy was just afraid of what it&nbsp;
had unleashed on an unsuspecting Foundation…&nbsp;

00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:49.800
Initial testing with the offspring creature&nbsp;
revealed it was perfectly healthy and seemingly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:55.080
very much unlike its predecessor. Until any&nbsp;
official SCP Foundation designation number&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.080 --> 00:09:02.400
could be assigned, the team examining it took to&nbsp;
calling it ‘SCP-096 Junior’ or shortened to simply&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:06.720
‘Junior’ for simplicity. Junior regarded&nbsp;
the Foundation scientists with curiosity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.720 --> 00:09:11.700
intrigued by them as well as their surroundings,&nbsp;
picking up medical instruments before very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:15.960
carefully placing them back where it found them,&nbsp;
treating every item it touched like they had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.960 --> 00:09:21.360
been made of the finest, most delicate glass.
One of the researchers likened its movements to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:26.820
that of a lemur, or other similar primates, but&nbsp;
with the reserved, timid, and docile nature of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:30.300
a well-domesticated pet.
That was at first.&nbsp;

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:35.700
Naturally, the SCP Foundation being the&nbsp;
organization that it is, there quickly became&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:43.140
an interest in whether Junior displayed the same&nbsp;
anomalous traits as SCP-096. Call it curiosity or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:48.600
caution, they wanted to know if it would react the&nbsp;
same way when observed without the protection of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:54.720
SCRAMBLE goggles. So, a test was devised, seating&nbsp;
a member of D Class personnel in the same room as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.720 --> 00:10:00.360
Junior, and tasked only with looking at the Shy&nbsp;
Guy’s spawn. Everyone gathered with bated breath,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:05.220
the research team watching from an observation&nbsp;
deck, all of them wearing SCRAMBLE goggles to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.220 --> 00:10:10.200
blur Junior’s face. As a blindfolded D Class&nbsp;
was brought in and stood opposite Junior,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.200 --> 00:10:14.940
all of them already expected that the test&nbsp;
would unfold in a particular way. Which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.940 --> 00:10:20.820
made it all the more surprising when, as the D&nbsp;
Class’s blindfold was removed, nothing happened.&nbsp;

00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:25.740
Junior regarded the convict with the same&nbsp;
general curiosity as it had for everyone else,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.740 --> 00:10:32.700
but beyond that, showed no change in behavior.&nbsp;
No wild crying, no murderous rage state. Nothing.&nbsp;

00:10:32.700 --> 00:10:37.620
“Are we sure this is actually the Shy&nbsp;
Guy’s kid?” one of the researchers joked.&nbsp;

00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:42.240
With the test concluded – and then repeated&nbsp;
a few extra times for good measure – Junior&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:48.960
was deemed a ‘Safe’ class anomaly. Much like&nbsp;
SCP-999 or Josie the Half-Cat, it was decided&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:54.180
that Junior be allowed to wander freely around&nbsp;
the facility. While initially a little unnerving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.180 --> 00:10:59.040
to some staff when they first saw him without&nbsp;
goggles, people quickly warmed to Junior. He was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:03.900
like a small monkey from a safari park, although&nbsp;
with the added benefit of not stealing anyone’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:10.620
iPhone or wallet. At least, until shortly after.
Around nearly a month had passed since Junior’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.620 --> 00:11:17.880
birth, and since then, an odd change had been&nbsp;
noted in SCP-096. The Shy Guy seemed calmer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.880 --> 00:11:23.400
more at ease, and far less anxious. What’s more,&nbsp;
researchers discovered that, for the first time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.400 --> 00:11:29.820
ever… he could be observed. However, before they&nbsp;
could investigate further, all hell broke loose.&nbsp;

00:11:29.820 --> 00:11:35.040
It started in the holding cells where D Class&nbsp;
were housed, initially written off as fights&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:39.780
between inmates that got a little too out of hand.&nbsp;
But soon, the Foundation’s own personnel started&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:39.780 --> 00:11:45.180
to violently attack each other. It was sparked&nbsp;
at random, a state of animalistic rage that was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:49.260
focused on their fellow staff members.&nbsp;
The people they worked with… the people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:49.260 --> 00:11:54.780
who saw them every day. And it didn’t stop.
Those working at the facility were seemingly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.780 --> 00:12:00.240
possessed by an inescapable urge to harm those&nbsp;
around them, as if punishing each other for just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:05.280
looking at them. By the time a Mobile Task Force&nbsp;
was ordered to step in and diffuse the situation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:10.860
the scene they arrived to was one of utter chaos.
Further examination uncovered that those who had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:10.860 --> 00:12:15.840
seen Junior’s face had been exposed to an&nbsp;
anomalous effect. Looking at the creature&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:15.840 --> 00:12:22.680
gave the observer the same rageful reaction to&nbsp;
being observed as SCP-096; they were compelled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.680 --> 00:12:28.560
to kill anyone who saw them. However, most&nbsp;
insidiously, this didn’t seem to take effect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:34.140
instantly. In fact, those affected only entered&nbsp;
their collective rage state after everyone in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:34.140 --> 00:12:40.380
facility had interacted with Junior at least once.&nbsp;
Almost like it’d been waiting to infect everyone.&nbsp;

00:12:40.380 --> 00:12:44.160
While the remainder of the Foundation&nbsp;
mopped up the aftermath of the incident,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.160 --> 00:12:51.180
some theorized that SCP-096 had somehow expelled&nbsp;
all its self-consciousness, all its negative&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:51.180 --> 00:12:57.420
traits into its progeny. This was supposedly&nbsp;
why the Shy Guy seemed much calmer, so much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:57.420 --> 00:13:04.260
so that it could even be observed. Whether Junior&nbsp;
simply couldn’t contain all SCP-096’s negativity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:10.140
or intentionally spread it to everyone around&nbsp;
it, is unknown. The only solution to get things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:15.720
back to normal, was to put the Shy Guy’s&nbsp;
self-consciousness back where it came from.&nbsp;

00:13:15.720 --> 00:13:24.120
Now go and check out “SCP-096 VS SCP-343”&nbsp;
and “SCP-096 VS SCP-106” for more!

